"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KJQ2NM0R1S09256\",\"title\":\"Bigadan - BioCCS — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Bigadan - BioCCS\",\"Bigadan\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"2HKF\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Apr 2026 to 31 Dec 2032\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"2HKF\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.4\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[],\"tables\":[],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://bigadan.com\",\"t\":\"Bigadan\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biogenic-capture-and-storage/1.4\",\"t\":\"Biogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.4\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1KEVKS1RX1S0H8K9\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nBigadan - BioCCS\\nBigadan\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n2HKF\\nCrediting period\\n01 Apr 2026 to 31 Dec 2032\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiogenic Carbon Capture and Storage v1.4\\nSummary\\n\\nKalundborg Bioenergy, owned by Bigadan, deploys full-scale biogenic CO₂ capture. Industrial and agricultural waste streams are converted into renewable bioenergy, while a dedicated capture unit extracts and purifies resulting biogenic CO₂. The liquefied CO₂ is transported and permanently stored offshore in geological storage in the North Sea.\\n\\nDenmark\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nNo project documents yet\\nNo documents have been submitted for this project\"}"